A place has time only while its virtual time is at or behind the clock.
A thread that ran a count ahead of its units would wait a span for them where it should start its next request;
a place has time while its virtual time lies at most a span ahead of the clock.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place waits on another queue than its virtual time says
Report: a turn its own units give time runs no request on them
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -220,7 +220,7 @@ static uint32_t place_core(const struct place *p)
  */
 static bool has_time(const struct place *payer, const struct place *p, uint64_t now)
 {
-    return place_units(payer) != 0 && (request_open(payer, p) || payer->vt <= now + place_span(payer));
+    return place_units(payer) != 0 && (request_open(payer, p) || payer->vt <= now);
 }
 
 /* The count a place's units give it time again at, with no request open: its virtual time less its span. */
